@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `il07-pipeline`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07: INDEPENDENT TESTS, by fid-il-07 (an independent test author).
--
-- Every expected value below was decided from the Hebrew sources, the enacted
-- amending Laws and official published figures, and written down in
-- DECIDED-ANSWERS.md (finished 2026-10-06T23:46:05Z) BEFORE any .l4 file of this
-- encoding was opened. The household numbers H01-H47 are that file's. Nothing
-- here is taken from the encoder's il07-tests.l4 except the shape of its inputs.
--
-- A failing (or refused) assertion is a finding, listed in
-- INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md. No expected value has been edited to match what the
-- capstone computes. Assertions added after the encoding was seen are marked
-- "ADDED AFTER SEEING THE ENCODING" and are recorded in DECIDED-ANSWERS.md's
-- appended section.
--
-- My figures, all from the sources (DECIDED-ANSWERS.md section 0-1):
--   ITO s 121(b)(1), (a): 10% to 84,120; 14% to 120,720; 20% to 228,000;
--     31% to 301,200; 35% to 560,280; 47% above.  s 121B: 3% above 721,560.
--   ITO s 33A credit point 2,904 a year; ss 34, 36, 36A: 2 + 1/4 (+ 1/2 woman).
--   ITO s 66(c)(4) mother / (5) father children's points, claimed by the sole
--     earner under s 66(c)(1A).
--   NII s 342(c)(1), Schedule J column D (Amendment 252 s 7; 2025 Budget-year Law
--     s 19(6)): 1.04% up to 7,703; 7.00% (the printed total) above, up to 51,910.
--   NII ss 66, 67(b), 68, s 1 basic amounts 2026: 173 / 219 / 219 / 219 / 173.
--   NII s 72 (not encoded by any row) for the months of birth and of an 18th
--     birthday.
--   Health: an input, from the Institute's published 3.23% / 5.17%.
--   Net = salary - tax/12 - NI - health + allowance.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 — independent tests (fid-il-07)`

§§ `Builders (inputs only)`

-- A resident adult employee paid the same salary in every month of 2026, with no
-- credit or deduction beyond the composed rows', to whom the full adult minimum
-- wage applies. A woman's Schedule A1 Part D age (an input the capstone needs
-- for NII s 342(c)(2)) is given as 70 years, which does not bind at age 36.
GIVEN `n` IS A STRING
      `f` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 earner`
`fid: an earner` `n` `, a woman:` `f` `, paid` `s` MEANS
    `IL-07 earner` WITH
        `the earner's name`                                                              IS `n`
        `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS `f`
        `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS YMD 1990 1 1
        `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS `s`
        `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
        `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
        `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
        `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
        `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
        `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
        `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS
            IF `f` THEN JUST 840 ELSE NOTHING
        `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE

-- The same earner with a credit or deduction under a provision no row encodes
-- (H41 pension s 45A/s 47; H42 immigrant s 35).
GIVEN e IS AN `IL-07 earner`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 earner`
`fid: with an unencoded credit or deduction,` e MEANS
    `IL-07 earner` WITH
        `the earner's name`                                                              IS e's `the earner's name`
        `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS e's `the earner is a woman`
        `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS e's `the earner's date of birth`
        `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS e's `the earner's monthly salary`
        `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
        `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
        `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
        `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
        `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
        `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
        `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS
            e's `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman`
        `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS FALSE

-- H43: a non-resident under both Laws.
GIVEN e IS AN `IL-07 earner`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 earner`
`fid: not resident,` e MEANS
    `IL-07 earner` WITH
        `the earner's name`                                                              IS e's `the earner's name`
        `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS e's `the earner is a woman`
        `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS e's `the earner's date of birth`
        `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS e's `the earner's monthly salary`
        `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
        `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS FALSE
        `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
        `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS FALSE
        `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS FALSE
        `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
        `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS
            e's `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman`
        `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE

-- H45b: the full adult minimum wage is not said to apply.
GIVEN e IS AN `IL-07 earner`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 earner`
`fid: minimum wage not the full adult figure,` e MEANS
    `IL-07 earner` WITH
        `the earner's name`                                                              IS e's `the earner's name`
        `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS e's `the earner is a woman`
        `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS e's `the earner's date of birth`
        `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS e's `the earner's monthly salary`
        `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
        `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
        `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
        `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
        `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
        `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS FALSE
        `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS
            e's `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman`
        `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE

-- A wife at home: no income; a "housewife" under NII s 238, so not insured
-- under Chapter 11 (NII s 65 "מבוטח" excludes her).
`fid: a wife at home` MEANS
    `IL-07 spouse` WITH
        `the spouse's name`                                                              IS "Wife"
        `the spouse is a woman`                                                          IS TRUE
        `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                    IS 0
        `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS FALSE
        `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS TRUE
        `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE

-- A husband at home: no income; insured under Chapter 11.
`fid: a husband at home` MEANS
    `IL-07 spouse` WITH
        `the spouse's name`                                                              IS "Husband"
        `the spouse is a woman`                                                          IS FALSE
        `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                    IS 0
        `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
        `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE

-- The sole earner is the registered spouse (ITO s 64B) and claims the separate
-- calculation of s 66(c)(1A); no s 37 point (no "יחיד מוטב").
GIVEN `sp` IS AN `IL-07 spouse`
GIVETH A MAYBE `IL-07 couple`
`fid: married to` `sp` MEANS
    JUST (`IL-07 couple` WITH
        `the earner's spouse`                                                            IS `sp`
        `the earner is the registered spouse`                                            IS TRUE
        `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion` IS TRUE
        `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS FALSE)

-- Each child carries its own name: row IL-06 tells children apart by name, and
-- two children of one name are "a problem with the facts" there (my first run
-- named every child "Child"; see INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md, finding M1).
GIVEN `nm` IS A STRING
      `d`  IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `IL-07 child`
`fid: a child` `nm` `, born` `d` MEANS
    `IL-07 child` WITH
        `the child's name`                                                               IS `nm`
        `the child's date of birth`                                                      IS `d`
        `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
      `m` IS A NUMBER
      `e` IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `c` IS A MAYBE `IL-07 couple`
      `k` IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `hl` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 household in a month`
`fid: in` `y` `/` `m` `,` `e` `,` `c` `,` `k` `, health` `hl` MEANS
    `IL-07 household in a month` WITH
        `the year of the month`                                                          IS `y`
        `the month of the year`                                                          IS `m`
        `the earner`                                                                     IS `e`
        `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`                                         IS `c`
        `the children of the household`                                                  IS `k`
        `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month`    IS `hl`


§§ `Group A — no children; every bracket and contribution threshold`

